HOW FILES INTERACT WITH EACH OTHER 

cli.js its user-interfaces layers , its defines the commands like create, list, status, show, and delete. Calls TaskManager amd Displays success, failure or formatted task output 

app.js its the coodrinator layer, It exposese operations such as createTask() and updateTaskStatus(), Converts or Validates input, Creates Task object, Desides which storage operations to call

modelS.js its the domain layer , it defines the task class, Task status, TaskPriority and Behaviour asuch as update(), markAsDone(), isOverDue()

storage.js its persistence layer. It keeps tasks in memory, Loads tasks from tasks.json, Saves tasks to tasks.json, And adds, retrieves, updates, filters, and deletes tasks

EXTERNAL DEPENDENCIES 
commander in cli.js for command-line parsing
uuid in models.js for generating task IDs 
Node.js fs in srorage.js for reading and writing files
Node.js path is used by the storage implementation 
tasks.json as local persistent storage 

