    H --> I[JSON.stringify]
    I --> J[tasks.json]

TASK CHANGES THROUGH COMPLETION 
flows through these stages 
 1. cli.js parses the command-line aguments 
 2. it calls taskManager.createTask(...)
 3. app.js recieves the title, description, priority, due data string, and tags 
 4. app.js converts the due date string into a JS Date
 5. models.js creates a Task object 
 6. The construction generates and ID  and sets defaults such as 
     - status = TODO 
     - createdAt 
     - updatedAt 
     - completedAt = null
 7. storage.js places the task in this.task 
 8. save() converts the in-memory object to JSON and writes it to tasks.json 
 9. The task ID travels back to cli.js, which prints a success message 

POTENTIAL FAILURE 
 - invalid date input in app.js 
 - Missing or malformed tasks.json
 - File read permission or file-not-found problems 
 - invalid JSON structure 
 - file write permission or disk errors 
 - Missing task IDs during retrieval, updates, or deletion 
 - invalid priority or status value 
 - invalid task data loaded from JSON fils 

HOW THE APPLICATION PERSIST THE CHANGES 
 - Invalid dates return null from createTask()
 - missing files are tolerated because load() only reads when files exists
 - Malformes saved data is caught and logged 
 - Missing task IDs generally return undefined or false


